# Secrets. .gitignore does NOT apply to the Docker build context, so without
# these two lines .env — which holds the real Google client secret and the
# database password — would be copied straight into the image, where anyone who
# can pull it can read it back out. .env.example carries only placeholders and is
# harmless, but nothing needs it either.
.env
.env.properties
.env.example

# Built on the host. The image compiles from source in its own stage, so any
# target/ lying around is dead weight in the context — and a stale jar in it
# would be genuinely confusing.
target/

# Version control and tooling: none of it is needed to build or run, and .git in
# particular can be large enough to slow the context upload noticeably.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.vscode/

# The wrapper is unused: the build stage has Maven already.
.mvn/
mvnw
mvnw.cmd

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
HELP.md
README.md
